      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-330877",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{\u2032}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nUsing the method of variation of parameters, we wish to find a particular solution in the form ${x}_{p}(t)=\u03a6u(t),$ where $\u03a6$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system and $u(t)$ is a column vector of functions to be determined. A derivation of the formula for ${x}_{p}(t)$ is given below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=\u03a6u(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}^{\u2032}(t)=\u03a6{u}^{\u2032}(t)+{\u03a6}^{\u2032}u(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $\u03a6{u}^{\u2032}(t)+{\u03a6}^{\u2032}u(t)=A\u03a6u(t)+f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${\u03a6}^{\u2032}=A\u03a6$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $\u03a6{u}^{\u2032}(t)=f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${u}^{\u2032}(t)={\u03a6}^{-1}(t)f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $u(t)=\\int {\u03a6}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=\u03a6\\int {\u03a6}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from the fact that {{field-1}} matrix.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L5}$ by {{field-2}} both sides of the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by {{field-3}} both sides of the equation."
    },
